ompig-slim
==========

This personal coding harness links PiG v0.7.0 as a Go library, with local
feature ports in vendor/github.com/MichaelKinsy/PiG. PiG is Copyright Michael
Kinsy, distributed under MIT. The original PiG notices are retained in that
module's LICENSE and NOTICE.

PiG implements Pi's coding-agent behavior. Pi is Copyright (c) 2025 Mario
Zechner, MIT. Personal features were translated from tmih06's omp-slim fork
at ba23ed9c3 and its working-tree refinements observed during this migration.

Provider authentication, transport, and quota behavior incorporates native
translations of oh-my-pi 18.16.0 code, Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner,
Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Can Bölük, Copyright (c) 2026 Stencil Labs, Inc., MIT.
The full permission notice is reproduced in LICENSE.

This project is not an official release of PiG, Pi, or oh-my-pi. Their
maintainers do not endorse this personal distribution. Other dependency
license notices remain alongside their sources in vendor/. Release archives
include those notices as well as PiG's embedded third-party notices.

The built-in subagent feature translates tintinweb/pi-subagents, Copyright
(c) 2026 tintinweb, MIT, at commit 50460b5df6934c4237983a504808a04ee0f8a0a0.
Its license is retained at vendor/github.com/MichaelKinsy/PiG/internal/subagents/LICENSE.

The native Agent Hub ports the oh-my-pi Agent Hub overlay, projection, and
renderer from can1357/oh-my-pi at commit
f2b795ba747b23d42052184d822b41e3d01357cc (MIT).
The upstream copyright and permission notice are reproduced in LICENSE.

The bundled theme palettes in
vendor/github.com/MichaelKinsy/PiG/tui/theme_palettes.json are copied from
oh-my-pi's packages/tui/src/theme/defaults.json (MIT). The upstream copyright
and permission notice are reproduced in LICENSE.
